Original 1735 dispositions: 1014 PASS, 44 compiler-failure, 17 FP-deferred,
659 not-applicable, 1 oracle-unusable. Those historical totals are unchanged.

The 44 original compiler-failure identities reconcile as:
  7 unchanged originals subsequently PASS in targeted replay;
  30 source/argv-bound named FP deferrals (11 binary128, 1 binary16,
     9 floating-complex, 9 floating-vector);
  5 source/argv-bound evidenced not-applicable originals;
  2 OPEN originals: LARGE floyd-warshall timeout and pr23135 integer-vector UB.
This is not 1049 fresh passes, not a final-compiler campaign, and not evidence
that all remaining failures are floating point. Deferred implementations and
fresh full acceptance remain open in TODO L02-L05, L10, B02 and B10.

Validation uses the existing llvm-test-suite.py program_disposition function
on each frozen row and the unchanged source checkout. All 35 reviewed rows
pass exact originalArguments, source SHA-256 and evidence-file validation.
The remaining 9 historical failures correctly stay compiler-failure when
only that old row is classified: subsequent PASS requires actual later-run
evidence, not a new waiver. Eight obsolete pre-scalar-FP reviews were removed
(the seven repaired originals plus floyd-warshall); the regression test first
fails eight subcases and then passes. No old receipt was rewritten.

Evidence keys (paths relative to tests/fixtures unless stated otherwise):
S = benchmark-small-frontier.out: unchanged-source/argv native replay;
    compare-fp-1/4/pr50310 compiler 3d4dac62...3b5e3;
    compare-fp-3 compiler b625baf1...21a9b;
    20020720-1 compiler b5428a5c...1fc32. No link_error stubs.
P = linear-block-binding.out: unchanged LARGE output/hash/exit-status checks,
    compiler 8e87fa4e...59007; lu 59.2533s, ludcmp 48.8197s, original limit 60s.
    The small timing margin is not a stable performance guarantee.
F = llvm-floating-value-paths.out, llvm-floating-builtins.out, and the exact
    source/argv/evidence/deferredFeatures row in
    tests/contracts/benchmark-program-dispositions.json. NEON additionally S.
D = llvm-declaration-frontier.out plus source/argv-bound disposition: the
    approved GNU11 implicit-declaration boundary, not oracle rejection.
U = llvm-uninitialized-original.out: positive uninitialized-read observations
    in independently compiled GCC/Clang UBSan-instrumented originals under
    Memcheck; plain Memcheck alone is NOT a positive control.
T = repeated-pointer-index.out: original LARGE still TIMEOUT at 60 seconds;
    repeated-pointer-index.c and linear-block-binding.c are small reductions.
V = llvm-vector-overflow-reduction.c/.out: integer lane signed multiplication
    exceeds INT_MAX; both interpreters E3004; original Clang instrumentation
    does not diagnose it. L10 remains NEEDS_RULE, not an approved exclusion.

